<section>
    <h3>Symfony already knew how to… replay</h3>
    <pre><code class="language-php" data-trim>
use Symfony\Component\HttpClient\MockHttpClient;
use Symfony\Component\HttpClient\Test\HarFileResponseFactory;

$client = new MockHttpClient(new HarFileResponseFactory(__DIR__.'/fixtures/api.har'));
    </code></pre>
    <ul style="font-size: 0.85em;">
        <li class="fragment"><code>HarFileResponseFactory</code> already exists in the component</li>
        <li class="fragment">But you have to produce the HAR file yourself</li>
        <li class="fragment">The <b>recording</b> half was missing</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="fragment callout">
        The recorder <b>builds on what is already there</b>: one HAR format, to record and to replay.
    </p>
    <aside class="notes">
        <p>Good news: Symfony could already replay a HAR file, with HarFileResponseFactory.</p>
        <p>[click] So replay already existed.</p>
        <p>[click] But you had to create the HAR file yourself. And clean it by hand.</p>
        <p>[click] The recording part was missing.</p>
        <p>[click] The recorder adds that missing part, with the same format. One format to record and to replay.</p>
    </aside>
</section>
